---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE, contentDescriptors, whatToExpect } from '../lib/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About the game"
  description="What this world is, what a game in it feels like, and what it is not."
  section="about"
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 pt-12 sm:px-8 sm:pt-16">
    <header class="max-w-2xl">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 text-[clamp(2.2rem,5vw,3.2rem)]">About the game</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[1.18rem] text-ash">
        {SITE.name} is a world for fantasy tabletop roleplaying. Replace this page's prose with the
        world's own; the tone list below comes from the world's site vocabulary.
      </p>
      <span class="rule-ember mt-6"></span>
    </header>

    <div class="mt-12 grid gap-x-14 gap-y-12 md:grid-cols-[minmax(0,42rem)_13rem]">
      <div class="prose-hollow max-w-[64ch]">
        <h2>What this site is</h2>
        <p>
          A world bible, written in the open, and the codex a game master can run from. Note however that 
          it is the player facing portion of the codex. It is not a
          campaign and it is not a novel: it is the world several campaigns will share, designed so
          that the politics, the magic and the monsters all trace back to the same history.
        </p>
        <p>
          The rules and engine are in development. The world is not waiting for them — it is built to be played
          in with whatever system you bring. It is being written as the first campaign world for the 
          <em> Mythical Forge game engine</em>. A platform to support TTRPG style solo (initially) game play.
          Its not a 3D FPS style engine, but rather one that acts as a GM for pen and paper style fantasy RPG's.
        </p>

        <h2>What a game feels like</h2>
        <p>
          You are not heroes arriving to save a world. You are people with debts, in a place where
          water is money, where every road ends at a gate someone else controls, and where the
          powerful have good reasons to keep you ignorant.
        </p>
        <p>
          The interesting decisions are not good against evil. They are who eats, who is owed, who is
          told, and which of two people you disappoint.
        </p>

        <h2>The tone, plainly</h2>
        <ul>
          {whatToExpect.map((line) => <li>{line}</li>)}
        </ul>

        <h2>Content</h2>
        <p>
          {SITE.name} campaigns use the content descriptors of
          <strong>{contentDescriptors.join(', ')}</strong> unless a campaign says otherwise. The horror
          is quiet and it is mostly people; the violence is not glamorous; the world is not fair.
        </p>

        <h2>What is not here</h2>
        <p>
          No secrets. Everything on this site is knowledge a resident of the world could have —
          official history, common belief, rumour, and the disagreements between them. The truth
          underneath is the part a campaign is for.
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="marginalia md:border-l md:border-[var(--rule)] md:pl-5">
        <p class="eyebrow mb-2">In one line</p>
        <p>
          A grim dark world of failing water and long grudges, where the world cannot be saved but
          the people in it can still be helped — or not.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-6 eyebrow mb-2">Status</p>
        <p>
          A living draft. Names are working titles; entries change; the
          <a href="/changelog/" class="no-underline">changelog</a> says what did.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-6 eyebrow mb-2">Credit</p>
        <p>
          Written and built by {SITE.author}. {SITE.license}
        </p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
